WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.370
ERIC: I think college is meant
to be a time when you decide

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.060
who you are and what you're
going to do with the person

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.216
that you are.

00:00:12.216 --> 00:00:14.870
DOMINIC: Trying to understand
truth bonds people together

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.840
in a way which very
few other things do.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.300
JACKIE: I knew I wanted
to go to a college that

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.820
would be spiritually
edifying, a place that

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.690
would be not safe for my faith
but a safe place to grow.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.720
CORINNE: There's always
this collaboration

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.000
of students just getting
together, supporting

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.550
one another, wanting to be
the best that we can be.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.970
ERIC: The liberal
arts are not as

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.740
much about gathering
information as they

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.410
are learning to be the
right kind of person to land

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.080
on your feet.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.750
HANNAH: The core
curriculum has been

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.975
essential to really see the
world as a complete picture.

00:00:47.975 --> 00:00:49.850
JACKIE: The professors
don't see the students

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.020
as bodies in the desks.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.068
They really see minds to
train and souls to cultivate.

00:00:56.068 --> 00:00:58.610
DOMINIC: College is meant to be
a place where we are prepared

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.740
for the rest of our
lives, where we are formed

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.950
and we are shaped in order
to act as good human beings

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:07.660
with an idea of the true and
the good and the beautiful.

